import{_ as t,o as i,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 541 | Historical-Reversal Simulation | Generic Reversal Trajectory of Predatory-School Civilizations","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 541 | Historical-Reversal Simulation | Generic Reversal Trajectory of Predatory-School Civilizations","no":541,"module":3,"tags":["Historical-Reversal Simulation","Predatory School","Generic Trajectory","Structural Inevitability","Quest-Domain Simulation Review"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis","84-Archaeology Protocol General Outline","87-Knowledge-Only Return Principle","15-Energy-Cycle-and-Transformation Law"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0541_模块3-历史倒车模拟-掠夺派文明的通用倒车轨迹.md","filePath":"en/0541_模块3-历史倒车模拟-掠夺派文明的通用倒车轨迹.md"}'),a={name:"en/0541_模块3-历史倒车模拟-掠夺派文明的通用倒车轨迹.md"};function r(s,e,l,c,d,h){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-541-historical-reversal-simulation-generic-reversal-trajectory-of-predatory-school-civilizations" tabindex="-1">Entry 541 | Historical-Reversal Simulation | Generic Reversal Trajectory of Predatory-School Civilizations <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-541-historical-reversal-simulation-generic-reversal-trajectory-of-predatory-school-civilizations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 541 | Historical-Reversal Simulation | Generic Reversal Trajectory of Predatory-School Civilizations&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 3 · Dual-Track Time Domain Civilizational-Experience System | Benchmark base: Documents 04, 84, 87, 15</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-strip-off-each-one-s-skin-all-predatory-school-civilizations-share-the-same-skeleton" tabindex="-1">Introduction: strip off each one&#39;s skin, all predatory-school civilizations share the same skeleton <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-strip-off-each-one-s-skin-all-predatory-school-civilizations-share-the-same-skeleton" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: strip off each one&#39;s skin, all predatory-school civilizations share the same skeleton&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The preceding seven reversal sandboxes, from Tang Luo, Shrouding-the-Heavens, Perfect World, Douluo, Dragon Ball to Wilderness, vary in surface: some collapse in bounty vacuum, some perish in Almighty burial, some dry in ecological exhaustion, some hollow in power inflation. But stacking their time-axis curves together, researchers found an unsettling fact — <strong>strip off each one&#39;s skin, all predatory-school civilizations share the same skeleton, sliding along the same generic reversal trajectory.</strong> This entry distills that generic trajectory as the master diagnostic model for subsequent Civilizational Correction Engineering.</p><p>Six top-level axioms are the distillation&#39;s highest criteria: anti-predation axiom is this trajectory&#39;s fundamental reason for existing; republican axiom of Myriad Races is its antidote; collective ascension axiom is its mirror negative; causal self-discipline axiom constrains all distillation to run only in Quest-Sediment-Domain sandboxes; law-first axiom requires the generic trajectory as a causal model defined first by law, not altered by individual planes&#39; accidental performance. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-generic-skeleton-three-segments-five-nodes" tabindex="-1">I. Generic Skeleton: Three Segments, Five Nodes <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-generic-skeleton-three-segments-five-nodes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Generic Skeleton: Three Segments, Five Nodes&quot;">​</a></h2><p>After cross-sandbox comparison, predatory-school civilization&#39;s reversal compresses into a &quot;three-segment five-node&quot; generic model:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Segment</th><th>Node</th><th>Generic Mechanism</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Segment 1: Eating Stock</td><td>① Predatory Start</td><td>Opens with slaughter, devouring, enclosure; energy from stock</td></tr><tr><td>Segment 1</td><td>② Monopoly Reinforcement</td><td>Great Dao secretly hoarded, classes stratified; the strong lock the evolution channel</td></tr><tr><td>Segment 2: Turning Inward</td><td>③ Stock Peaks</td><td>Predatable objects deplete; external dividends vanish</td></tr><tr><td>Segment 2</td><td>④ Turn Inward</td><td>Predation target shifts from outside to inside; mutual slaughter begins</td></tr><tr><td>Segment 3: Total Settlement</td><td>⑤ Reversal Erupts</td><td>Institutions collapse, knowledge breaks, ecosystems wither; slide along time axis</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Five nodes in each concrete plane have different names (Tang Luo calls it &quot;bounty vacuum,&quot; Shrouding-the-Heavens &quot;Dark Turmoil,&quot; Douluo &quot;spirit-beast extinction,&quot; Wilderness &quot;spirit-vein depletion&quot;), but the mechanism is identical. This is precisely the law-first axiom&#39;s victory: <strong>setting self-consistency over plot convenience; structure does not change because of story packaging.</strong></p><h2 id="ii-why-generic-three-invariants" tabindex="-1">II. Why &quot;Generic&quot;: Three Invariants <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-generic-three-invariants" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why &quot;Generic&quot;: Three Invariants&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The generic trajectory holds cross-plane because predatory-school civilizations share three invariants:</p><ol><li><strong>Energy direction invariant</strong>: always &quot;extract — concentrate — consume,&quot; not &quot;develop — cycle — increment.&quot; Once energy direction is extraction, stock bottoming is a matter of time, not luck.</li><li><strong>Knowledge direction invariant</strong>: always &quot;secret hoard — monopolize — buried with the strong,&quot; not &quot;open — network — retain across generations.&quot; Once knowledge is secretly hoarded, generation break is a matter of time.</li><li><strong>Governance direction invariant</strong>: always &quot;strong-person backstop — class stratification — no one corrects errors,&quot; not &quot;four-power checks — Alaya records — continuous review.&quot; Once governance relies on a strong person, after reversal no one slams the brakes.</li></ol><p>Three invariants are like three gravitational lines, pulling all predatory-school civilizations toward the same sliding curve. This is why changing protagonist, changing map, changing packaging cannot save them — same soup, different medicine.</p><h2 id="iii-mirror-comparison-of-generic-trajectory-and-symbiotic-civilization" tabindex="-1">III. Mirror Comparison of Generic Trajectory and Symbiotic Civilization <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-mirror-comparison-of-generic-trajectory-and-symbiotic-civilization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Mirror Comparison of Generic Trajectory and Symbiotic Civilization&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Juxtaposing the generic trajectory and the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s time vector yields a clean set of mirrors:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Predatory Generic Trajectory</th><th>Anchor Symbiotic Civilization</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Energy</td><td>Extract stock</td><td>Develop increments; Myriad-Rank origin bidirectional cycle</td></tr><tr><td>Knowledge</td><td>Secret hoard, monopolize</td><td>Great Dao all-level open; Alaya network-wide sharing</td></tr><tr><td>Governance</td><td>Strong-person backstop</td><td>Four-power checks; Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision</td></tr><tr><td>Time</td><td>Thinner the more used</td><td>Dual-track sutured; thicker the more used</td></tr><tr><td>Endgame</td><td>Total settlement reversal</td><td>Collective ascension; always positive</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The mirror shows: whether a civilization reverses depends not on how many enemies it meets, or whether geniuses appear, but on what direction it sets these three invariants.</p><h2 id="iv-review-results-a-generic-reversal-diagnostic-table" tabindex="-1">IV. Review Results: A Generic Reversal Diagnostic Table <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-review-results-a-generic-reversal-diagnostic-table" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Review Results: A Generic Reversal Diagnostic Table&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The sandbox compresses five nodes into a diagnostic table usable on any plane:</p><ul><li><strong>① Predatory-start self-check</strong>: does this civilization&#39;s core energy come from slaughter and devouring?</li><li><strong>② Monopoly-reinforcement self-check</strong>: are the Great Dao and cultivation grounds secretly hoarded and enclosed by a few?</li><li><strong>③ Stock-peak self-check</strong>: are externally predatable objects decreasing?</li><li><strong>④ Turn-inward self-check</strong>: have &quot;hunter hunts hunter&quot; involution signs appeared?</li><li><strong>⑤ Reversal-eruption self-check</strong>: are institutions, knowledge, ecosystems showing irreversible decline?</li></ul><p>Any one lighting a red light indicates the civilization has slid into some node of the generic trajectory; immediately launch Civilizational Correction Engineering (from Entry 542). This table all comes from cross-plane induction in isolated sandboxes, following the &quot;Knowledge-Only Return Principle.&quot;</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: the generic trajectory once-for-all explains the civilizational-level waste of &quot;eat stock — total settlement,&quot; proving predation loses on the time axis</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: the five-node model is predatory school&#39;s pathology slice — it is not occasional slip, but structural suicide</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo is just one concrete case of the five-node model; strip its skin, it shares the skeleton with Shrouding-the-Heavens, Douluo, Wilderness</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the diagnostic table applies to all beings of five gene lineages, showing no favoritism to any predatory civilization&#39;s &quot;specialty&quot;</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: three-segment five-node model, three invariants, generic diagnostic table all public, becoming the whole cosmos&#39;s public checkup tool</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The generic reversal trajectory of predatory-school civilizations is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s ultimate mathematical answer to &quot;can predation ultimately win&quot;: no. Not because some hero is not strong enough, or some plane not rich enough, but because &quot;eating stock, secretly hoarding knowledge, strong-person backstop&quot; — these three invariants, on a long enough time axis, inevitably pull any civilization toward total settlement. Acknowledging this generic trajectory is not pessimism, but using it in reverse as a map: as long as the three invariants&#39; directions are corrected one by one, any civilization can turn from the sliding curve to the ascension curve. This, is what Civilizational Correction Engineering must do.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis</a> · <a href="./84-考古协议总纲.html">84-Archaeology Protocol General Outline</a> · <a href="./87-仅回传知识原则.html">87-Knowledge-Only Return Principle</a> · <a href="./15-能量循环与转化法则.html">15-Energy-Cycle-and-Transformation Law</a></li></ul>',27)])])}const m=t(a,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
